---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ContactPerson } from "../components/ContactPerson";
import { ShareGroupMockup } from "../components/ShareGroupMockup";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>For contractors | Spokane Contractors</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Your neighbor dropped your name. Let’s make sure they drop your number, too. Free listing—no account, no lead fee."
    />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="how-it-works">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">For contractors</p>
    <h1>Your neighbor dropped your name. Let’s make sure they drop your number, too.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Most of your work comes from word of mouth. We turn a half-remembered
      name-drop into a paste-ready listing—so the recommendation reaches your
      phone.
    </p>

    <ShareGroupMockup origin="https://spokanelist.com" />

    <section>
      <h2>The usual thread</h2>
      <p>
        Someone asks for a plumber in a local Facebook group. A neighbor drops
        your name from memory. Then the pile-on starts: what’s their number? Do
        they have a website? Where are their Google reviews?
      </p>
      <p>
        The neighbor who meant to help goes hunting. The homeowner gets pulled
        into ads. You never get the call. The warm lead went cold.
      </p>
      <p>
        We package your trade, city, phone, website, and rating into one listing
        neighbors can paste. License sits on the page when we have it. The
        recommendation travels whole. A warm mention can turn into a ring.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How this works for your business</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Turn chats into a call</strong> because we put your details in
          one link neighbors can paste anywhere. A neighbor’s paste beats a cold
          Google search.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Stop bidding for your own leads</strong> because you pay zero
          lead fees. No bidding wars. No account to maintain.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Skip a second profile</strong> because we refresh from your{" "}
          <a href="https://business.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            Google Business Profile
          </a>
          . You keep Google current. We do the rest.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Let your reputation sell</strong> because your Google rating
          and review count travel with your name. No Maps screenshots.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The honest truth</h2>
      <p>
        This does not replace Google. It does not guarantee jobs. Your volume
        still depends on neighborhood word of mouth.
      </p>
      <p>
        The win is simple: cleaner referrals. More complete. No extra work from
        you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What your free listing includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          A shareable page with your name, trade, city, phone, and website.
        </li>
        <li>Google rating and review count when we have them from GBP.</li>
        <li>A listing link that keeps working when someone pastes it in chat.</li>
        <li>
          Updates from your Google Business Profile—you don’t manage a second
          profile here.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Keep GBP accurate, then <a href="/get-listed">request a listing</a> or a
        fix. We refresh as needed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>If you ever want a hand</h2>
      <p>
        Some local contractors ask for help getting more Google reviews, cleaning
        up a Business Profile, or putting up a simple website that matches this
        listing. If that’s useful, you’re welcome to write. If not, the directory
        stays free either way.
      </p>
      <ContactPerson />
    </section>

    <p class="how-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/get-listed">Request my listing</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/">Browse the directory</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
